  "facts": [
    "The Plabutsch Tunnel stretches nearly 10 kilometers, with its east section measuring 9,919 meters and west section 10,085 meters, making it one of Austria's longest road tunnels.",
    "Designed to divert traffic from Graz, the tunnel runs along the city's western flank, easing congestion and providing a smoother flow for commuters heading eastward.",
    "Completed in the early 2000s, the Plabutsch Tunnel showcases advanced engineering techniques, including precise alignment of its twin bores to accommodate Austria's challenging alpine terrain."
